The survey is written to `runs\Absolute_2026-09-28_02\sota\cycle-002\survey-1.json`.

Stage 2 runs once per synced pair, on the detection `select_detection` already chose. The other class-matched `source_index` values are dropped, and neither `PalletPoseStamped` nor the diagnostics publish them. The two early returns still publish nothing.

That one call is dominated by the chamfer grids. With the prior search, which is the common case unless the free cost is about 0.006233 m or lower, the frame does 45700 trimmed-mean evaluations of the 182-point prototype. Each evaluation copies the rotated contour, sorts all 182 distances, and keeps 164. OpenMP does not reduce that count.

The depth conversion, the full 640×480 face scan, the RANSAC copies, and the 561×350 distance transform all run once per detection and are smaller than that grid. A TensorRT stage 1 is a separate process; writing the already-stored indexes onto the pose or the failure diagnostic does not repeat the search.
